6|0@guns^1440856204#cujpdgd:mahansm$:I've got one I bought used that was a factory demonstrator and probably had a fairly high round count when I got it. It developed a problem with the forward cylinder lockup and I sent it back to S&amp;W for repair. While there they examined the gun and discovered severe erosion on the forcing cone which created a stress riser. This would have led to a crack developing and a failure in just the manner seen in the photo. S&amp;W told me to not shoot the gun until the barrel was replaced, and that for $150 they'd put a new barrel on while it was up there. I have the old barrel as a reminder to keep track of such things.
