0|0@guns^1440957401#cukxzsy:Long_rifle$:Free range lead. Zero cents. I cast at work, so no electricity cost. Cases are free, and at low pressures last this side of forever, I get hundreds of them from the range each year anyways. Wax lube. A buck a stick. Can do hundreds of bullets a stick. So about a quarter cent per bullet. Primers 3 bucks per hundred. So three cents. Powder about 18 bucks a pound. Can do 750 rounds easy per pound. Usually way more then that. But I'll give it that. 3.6 cents So using inflated numbers. You're right. 6.85 cents a round. So almost seven cents.... But I usually get primers in bulk, so they are closer to 2.50 per hundred. And powder in bulk. So usually closer to 16 bucks a pound. Which brings it down to 5 cents.
